":"point","class":"infinity","at":[0.0,6.2832]},{"kind":"point","class":"infinity","at":[4.7124,1.5708]},{"kind":"point","class":"infinity","at":[3.1416,0.0]}],"labels":[{"at":[0.0,6.2832],"text":"$i^+$","anchor":"b","class":"lab","dx":0,"dy":-6},{"at":[4.7124,1.5708],"text":"$i^0$","anchor":"l","class":"lab","dx":6,"dy":0},{"at":[3.1416,0.0],"text":"$i^-$","anchor":"tl","class":"lab","dx":4,"dy":3},{"at":[3.927,0.7854],"text":"$\\mathscr{I}^-$","anchor":"tl","class":"lab","dx":4,"dy":3},{"at":[2.3562,3.927],"text":"$\\mathscr{I}^+$","anchor":"bl","class":"lab","dx":5,"dy":-3},{"at":[2.8562,1.2854],"text":"the shell, $u = 0$","anchor":"tl","class":"small","dx":4,"dy":3},{"at":[0.0172,-1.5536],"text":"$r = q^2/2M$","anchor":"l","class":"small","dx":7,"dy":0}],"legend":[["fill","cover","before the shell, $m = M$ and $q = 0.96\\,M$: Reissner-Nordström"],["fill","cover2","after the shell, $m = q = 0$: flat"],["line","r","$r$ constant on the charged side: $0.3$, $0.5$, $0.85$, $1$, $1.15$, $1.6$, $2.5$ and $5\\,M$"],["line","r2","$r$ constant on the flat side: $0.5$, $1$, $2$ and $4\\,M$"],["line","t2","$u + r$ constant on the flat side"],["point","mark","the sphere $r = q^2/2M$ on the shell, where its energy density changes sign"],["line","surface","the shell $u = 0$, a light ray"],["line","centre","$r = 0$ on the flat side, a regular centre"],["line","horizon","$r = r_-$: the marginally trapped spheres and, where $u \\to -\\infty$, the edge of the chart"],["line","event","the white hole's horizon, from $i^-$ to the centre at $u = 2r_+$"],["zig","singular","$r = 0$ on the charged side, a timelike singularity, where the Kretschmann scalar diverges"],["line","scri","null infinity $\\mathscr{I}^\\pm$"]]},{"id":"bounce","label":"The shell turned back","box":[-0.35,5.0624,-6.5332,9.7248],"settings":"$M = 1$, the unit of every length, and $q = 0.96\\,M$, so that $r_+ = 1.28\\,M$, $r_- = 0.72\\,M$, and $q^2/2M = 0.46\\,M$.","input":"The falling shell as far as $r = q^2/2M$, and from there the leaving shell, with flat space inside both.","caption":["The same shell with the Lorentz force counted, each point in the diagram a 2-sphere. Amos Ori found in 1991 that charged null dust loses energy as it falls toward a like charge and turns round where its energy reaches zero, which for this shell is the sphere $r = q^2/2M = 0.46\\,M$, inside $r_-$. The shell falls in along a ray of constant $v$, turns at the mark, and leaves along a ray of constant $u$, through $r_-$ and $r_+$ of a white hole into another exterior, which it crosses to $\\mathscr{I}^+$. Its energy density is positive all the way.","Space inside the shell is flat throughout, so the centre is regular at every time, and the singularity of the charged region stands on the far side of it from the shell. The first exterior keeps its event horizon, and an observer who stays there sees the shell cross $r_+$ and nothing after. Outside the shell the metric is Reissner-Nordström's, read in ingoing coordinates before the turn and in outgoing coordinates after it."],"layers":[{"kind":"fill","class":"region","points":[[3.927,-2.3562],[0.0172,1.5536],[3.9442,5.4806],[4.7124,4.7124],[3.1416,3.1416],[3.1416,0.0],[4.7124,-1.5708]]},{"kind":"fill","class":"cover","points":[[3.927,-2.3562],[0.0172,1.5536],[3.9442,5.4806],[4.7124,4.7124],[3.1416,3.1416],[3.1416,0.0],[4.7124,-1.5708]]},{"kind":"fill","class":"region","points":[[0.0,-6.2832],[0.0172,1.5536],[3.9442,5.4806],[0.0,9.4248]]},{"kind":"fill","class":"cover2","points":[[0.0,-6.2832],[0.0172,1.5536],[3.9442,5.4806],[0.0,9.4248]]},{"kind":"line","class":"r2","points":[[0.0,-6.2832],[0.0193,-6.1288],[0.0484,-5.9468],[0.0855,-5.7514],[0.1232,-5.5764],[0.2069,-5.2293],[0.4192,-4.4049],[0.5073,-4.0156],[0.5461,-3.8179],[0.5803,-3.6214],[0.6101,-3.4276],[0.6755,-2.9571],[0.7056,-2.7709],[0.7466,-2.5789],[0.7752,-2.477],[0.8137,-2.3666],[0.8705,-2.2396],[0.9707,-2.0707],[1.7905,-1.1838],[2.0021,-0.9067],[2.0462,-0.7986],[2.0573,-0.7249],[2.0542,-0.66